/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  packing03_schulz_delft_0p10bar  --  a STRUCTURED-PACKING bed at total reflux, its HETP and
  pressure drop computed from the packing geometry (DEV.md 4c C329).

  THE TEST: Schulz, Rietfort, Jansen & Olujic, Chem. Eng. Trans. 69 (2018)
  763: FRI low-pressure column, 1.22 m, Montz-Pak A3-500M (corrugated wire
  gauze, 60 deg corrugations, installed area 478 m2/m3 measured on the
  delivered packing, void fraction ~0.92), bed 2.2 m (13 layers), p-xylene /
  o-xylene at total reflux, top pressure 0.10 bar.  HETP = bed height /
  Fenske stages between the distributor and the cross-sampler below the bed
  (section 2) -- the KPI `HETP` here is that definition.

  THE MODEL: the Delft model -- Olujic, Kamerbeek & de Graauw, Chem. Eng.
  Process. 38 (1999) 683, in the working form of Fair, Seibert, Behrens,
  Saraber & Olujic, IECR 39 (2000) 1788, Tables 2 and 4 -- the model Schulz
  et al. compare their own data with.  Complete wetting, holdup from the
  falling film, preloading drop from gas/liquid friction, gas/gas
  interaction and direction changes, the loading enhancement above F_G,lp;
  no per-packing constant.  The same bed integration as
  packing01/02 (Rocha-Bravo-Fair), which are this case's twins.

  WHY NOT BILLET & SCHULTES 1999 (the folder holds it): its Table 2b gives
  constants for Montz B1-200, B2-300, C1-200, C2-200 and no gauze packing --
  nothing for A3-500M.  The Delft model needs only the geometry.

  MEASURED INPUTS (Schulz section 2 and Table 1): diameter, bed height,
    installed area 478, void fraction 0.92, angle 60 deg, top pressure; the
    liquid viscosity 0.391 mPa s (Table 1 -- the package has no
    liquid-viscosity record for the xylenes).
  ESTIMATED: the corrugation base b = 11.5 mm and height h = 6.1 mm -- NOT
    printed by Schulz.  Taken with the base/height ratio of Montz B1-400
    (14.0/7.4 mm, Fair et al. 2000 Table 1) and scaled so that Fair's Eq 2,
    a_p = 4 s/(b h), returns the installed 478 m2/m3: h = 2.910/478 m.
    The element height 0.169 m is 2.2 m / 13 layers (Schulz section 2).
    The surface is unperforated (Schulz section 2): Omega = 0.
  ASSUMED: the reboiler liquid 0.2 mol fraction p-xylene, chosen so that the
    bed's mean liquid is near Table 1's average composition (0.54);
    the vapour molar flow is taken constant up the bed.
  ESTIMATED PROPERTIES: as listed in constant/thermoPhysPropDict, plus
    Wilke-Chang liquid diffusivity and Rackett liquid density.
  FITTED: nothing.  The 0.10 bar curve is the one the brief allowed to
    fit "what the correlation requires"; the Delft model requires no
    per-packing constant, so nothing was fitted at 0.10 bar either.
  HELD-OUT: every point of Schulz Fig. 2b at 0.10 bar (DIGITISED from the
    figure, 180 ppi raster; method and uncertainty in
    docs/design/c329-ratebased-first-delivery.md).
  IN-SAMPLE OR NOT: the Delft model has no per-packing constant; Fair et
    al. 2000 evaluated it on Montz B1/BSH sheet packings with
    cyclohexane/n-heptane -- not gauze, not this system.  Out of sample.

  THE SWEEP moves the boil-up F-factor (reboiler vapour on the tower area)
  and stops where the computed drop passes 10.25 mbar/m (Fair et al.
  2000's flooding-point pressure drop for structured packings).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       totalReflux;

        operation
        {
            P              0.10 bar;      // TOP pressure
            condenser      { type total; }

            totalReflux
            {
                fFactor        1.5;      // swept; (m/s)(kg/m3)^0.5, reboiler vapour on the tower area
                specifiedAt    reboiler;
                composition
                {
                    pXylene    0.2;
                    oXylene    0.80;
                }
            }

            packing
            {
                model             Delft;
                diameter          1.22 m;      // Schulz section 2
                height            2.2 m;       // Schulz section 2
                specificArea      478;         // m2/m3, installed (Schulz section 2)
                voidFraction      0.92;        // Schulz section 2
                corrugationAngle  60;          // deg (Schulz section 2)
                corrugationBase   0.01152 m;   // ESTIMATED: Montz B1-400 shape scaled to a_p = 478
                corrugationHeight 0.00609 m;   // ESTIMATED: as above
                elementHeight     0.169 m;     // 2.2 m / 13 layers (Schulz section 2)
                holeFraction      0;           // unperforated (Schulz section 2)
                lightKey          pXylene;
                liquidViscosity   3.91e-4;       // Pa s, Schulz Table 1
                segments          100;
            }
        }
    }
);
